4.3.1 Group Relative Policy Optimization
To reduce the training cost of RL, we adopt Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) [41], which avoids training a separate critic by estimating advantages from a group of rollouts. Given a training input x , GRPO samples a group of G candidate responses { y i } G i =1 from the old policy π θ old . The updated policy π θ is optimized by maximizing the following objective:
